## Navigation State Machine Flowchart

Every arrow below is a **legal transition**. If there's no arrow, the user **cannot** go there.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Intro : App launches

    Intro --> Onboarding : User clicks "Get Started" (no account)
    Intro --> Greeting : User has saved session (auto-login)

    Onboarding --> Intro : User clicks "Back"
    Onboarding --> Greeting : Signup/Login succeeds (API verified)

    Greeting --> Workspace : User clicks "Enter Workspace" (preflight done)
    Greeting --> Intro : User clicks "Sign Out"

    Workspace --> Intro : User clicks "Sign Out" (clears session)

    note right of Workspace
        DEAD END for "Back" button.
        There is NO path from Workspace back to Greeting.
        Back button is disabled here (stack is empty).
        The ONLY exit from Workspace is "Sign Out".
    end note

    note right of Greeting
        ONE-TIME GATE.
        Once user enters Workspace, Greeting
        is removed from the history stack.
        It cannot be revisited via "back".
    end note

    note right of Intro
        RESET POINT.
        Sign Out from anywhere lands here.
        Session storage is cleared.
        Fresh start.
    end note
```

### Guardrail Rules (Enforced in Code)

| From | To | Allowed? | How |
|------|-----|----------|-----|
| Workspace | Greeting | **NO** | Stack is cleared when entering workspace |
| Workspace | Onboarding | **NO** | Not in stack |
| Workspace | Intro | **Only via Sign Out** | Sign Out handler clears session + navigates |
| Greeting | Workspace | **Yes** | "Enter Workspace" button |
| Greeting | Intro | **Only via Sign Out** | Sign Out handler |
| Greeting | Onboarding | **NO** | Not in stack |
| Onboarding | Intro | **Yes** | Back button |
| Onboarding | Greeting | **Yes** | After successful auth API call |
| Intro | Onboarding | **Yes** | "Get Started" button |
| Intro | Greeting | **Yes** | Auto-login (valid saved session) |
| Any | Any via browser URL | **NO** | No URL-based routing. Pure state. |

### What Happens When User Presses "Back"

| Current Screen | Back Goes To | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Intro | Nothing (disabled) | This is the root. Can't go further back. |
| Onboarding | Intro | User went Intro → Onboarding. Logical. |
| Greeting | Nothing (disabled) | Stack was reset. Greeting is the start after auth. |
| Workspace | Nothing (disabled) | Stack was cleared on workspace entry. No going back. |

