#### [NEW] [KeyboardShortcutManager.tsx](file:///e:/All%20Projects%20and%20Editors/ERIS/frontend/src/context/KeyboardShortcutManager.tsx)

A context provider that:
1. Attaches one `keydown` listener to `window` on mount
2. Maintains a `Map<string, () => void>` of shortcut → action
3. Each shortcut combo is a string like `"ctrl+n"`, `"ctrl+shift+z"`, `"ctrl+["`, `"ctrl+]"`
4. On `keydown`, builds the combo string from the event, looks it up, calls `e.preventDefault()` + action
5. Exposes `registerShortcut(combo, action)` and `unregisterShortcut(combo)` for components to use
6. Also listens for **Mouse Button 4/5** (`mousedown` event, `event.button === 3` and `event.button === 4`)
   - Default: MB4 = `goBack()`, MB5 = `goForward()`
   - Stored in localStorage so user can remap later (future keyboard shortcuts settings UI)

**Default shortcuts:**

| Combo | Action | Note |
|-------|--------|------|
| `Ctrl+[` | Go Back (state machine) | Replaces Alt+← which conflicts with browser |
| `Ctrl+]` | Go Forward (state machine) | Replaces Alt+→ |
| `Ctrl+R` | Reload (state machine, not page) | `e.preventDefault()` to block browser |
| `Ctrl+N` | New Chat (clear messages) | |
| `Ctrl+D` | Toggle dark/light mode | |
| `Ctrl+B` | Toggle right sidebar | |
| `Ctrl+1` | Focus chat window | |
| `Ctrl+2` | Open workflow builder | |
| `Mouse4` | Go Back | Extra mouse button |
| `Mouse5` | Go Forward | Extra mouse button |

